{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>From Asher, his bread is fat.</b> Since he did not bless Gad, he says thus: even more so than Asher's, his bread shall be fat — that of Gad — because his land is a place of pasture for flocks." "<b>And he shall give</b> etc. Not because Asher's land is inferior; rather, he too, Asher, <b>shall yield royal delicacies</b>, and even so, Gad's land shall be better than it. Another interpretation: through Asher's land, the <b>bread of</b> Gad shall be <b>fat</b>, along with the rest of the tribes of Israel — for from Asher they would bring olive oil and fry their foods in oil. And so Moses said: 'Blessed of sons is Asher' — the children of Israel shall bless him and he shall be favorable to them, because he dips his foot in oil." "<b>And he shall yield royal delicacies.</b> A tribute of oil the kings of Israel would levy from him, to anoint with it and to pamper their flesh with it, as we have learned: and why do they anoint with it? Because it removes hair and softens the flesh."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:17.009399634Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}